  "notes": "Before it does any subordinate work, the subjunctive has jobs of its own: jussive/hortatory (let him, let us), deliberative (what am I to do?), and optative with utinam (would that…). Negatives take nē. Meeting a main-clause subjunctive, run this short list.",
